<%# THE HERO: heading, standfirst, actions and a picture of the product, composed as one block on the one
  dark field the page opens with.

  WHY DARK. The page used to open on paper and stay there: brand colour reached nothing but the buttons
  until the closing band 4,000px further down, and the product panel -- the only picture of the thing being
  sold -- was a white card on a white field, so it had no edge to separate it. On `lyn-ink` the panel is the
  brightest object on the screen without any decoration drawn around it, and the page gains the first beat of
  a rhythm it did not have: ink, then paper, then mist, then ink again at the close.

  THE EMPHASIS IS A RULE, NOT A STICKER. `highlight` is a phrase out of the heading that a translator may
  move to wherever their sentence actually turns, and it used to render as rotated magenta block -- white
  type on a coloured lozenge, which is a decade-old trope and was the only magenta on the site. It is now an
  underline in `lyn-blue`: the same emphasis, carried by the typography rather than by a shape behind it, and
  `whitespace-nowrap` keeps the marked phrase from breaking across two lines where the rule would read as two
  unrelated marks.

  THE PANEL IS THE PRODUCT, drawn in HTML rather than shipped as an image: a shared inbox with messages
  arriving from three channels, in the page's own language, which is the one thing that distinguishes this
  product from a chat widget. It is `aria-hidden` -- the names in it are illustrative, the heading and lede
  already carry the meaning, and a screen reader gains nothing from reading a drawing of a UI aloud.

  AND IT IS UPRIGHT. It used to be tilted a degree and a half over a second tilted plate, which needed a
  stacking context to paint at all, needed locale-dependent bottom padding so the badge cleared the dropping
  corner, and bought depth the dark field now gives for free.

  CHANNEL MARKS ARE NEUTRAL GLYPHS, not the channels' own logos. The channel is named in text beside each
  one, which is clearer, needs no trademark, and keeps the panel to one colour.
%>
<% primary = marketing_target_href(section['primary_target']) %>
<% secondary = marketing_target_href(section['secondary_target']) %>
<% heading = (page.heading.presence || page.title).to_s %>
<% highlight = section['highlight'].to_s %>

<section class="relative isolate overflow-hidden bg-lyn-ink">
  <%# THE FIELD. Two soft pools of brand colour rather than a flat slab -- indigo behind the panel, royal
      low and wide behind the heading -- so the band has depth without anything drawn on it. They are
      `-z-10` inside this isolated section, and `overflow-hidden` is what keeps a pool from putting a
      horizontal scrollbar on a narrow screen. %>
  <span class="absolute -right-40 -top-56 -z-10 size-[46rem] rounded-full bg-[radial-gradient(circle,rgba(91,91,240,0.42),transparent_62%)]" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="absolute -bottom-72 -left-32 -z-10 size-[42rem] rounded-full bg-[radial-gradient(circle,rgba(29,63,168,0.38),transparent_64%)]" aria-hidden="true"></span>

  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-center gap-14 px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_29rem] lg:gap-14 lg:py-28">
    <div class="motion-safe:animate-fade-in-up">
      <% if section['kicker'].present? %>
        <p class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-lyn-line-dark bg-lyn-ink/40 py-1.5 pe-4 ps-3 text-sm font-medium text-lyn-paper/80">
          <span class="size-2 rounded-full bg-lyn-blue" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <%= section['kicker'] %>
        </p>
      <% end %>

      <%# ONE H1, built from the row's own heading. The highlight is a literal phrase out of that string, so
          the two cannot disagree; a phrase that is not in the heading simply does not match and the heading
          renders whole. `split` on a literal needs no escaping of the needle, and every part is escaped by
          ERB on the way out.

          LEADING IS 1.18 AND NOT TIGHTER. This headline is set in IBM Plex Sans Arabic half the time, where
          the marks above and below the line need the room; display leading tuned on the Latin cut alone
          collides them. %>
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-balance text-[2.6rem] font-bold leading-[1.16] tracking-tight text-lyn-paper sm:text-[3.1rem] lg:text-[3.45rem]">
        <% if highlight.present? && heading.include?(highlight) %>
          <% before, after = heading.split(highlight, 2) %>
          <%= before %><span class="whitespace-nowrap underline decoration-lyn-blue decoration-[0.085em] underline-offset-[0.19em]"><%= highlight %></span><%= after %>
        <% else %>
          <%= heading %>
        <% end %>
      </h1>

      <% if page.lede.present? %>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-xl text-lg leading-[1.8] text-lyn-paper/70"><%= page.lede %></p>
      <% end %>

      <% if primary.present? || secondary.present? %>
        <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <% if primary.present? && section['primary_label'].present? %>
            <a href="<%= primary %>"
               class="inline-flex min-h-12 items-center rounded-xl bg-lyn-indigo px-7 text-base font-semibold text-lyn-paper shadow-[0_14px_38px_-12px_rgba(91,91,240,0.85)] transition-colors hover:bg-lyn-indigo-deep focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-lyn-blue">
              <%= section['primary_label'] %>
            </a>
          <% end %>
          <% if secondary.present? && section['secondary_label'].present? %>
            <a href="<%= secondary %>"
               class="inline-flex min-h-12 items-center rounded-xl border border-lyn-line-dark px-7 text-base font-semibold text-lyn-paper/90 transition-colors hover:border-lyn-blue hover:text-lyn-blue focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-lyn-blue">
              <%= section['secondary_label'] %>
            </a>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <div class="relative mx-auto w-full max-w-md pb-11 lg:max-w-none" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl bg-lyn-paper shadow-[0_44px_90px_-32px_rgba(0,0,0,0.7)]">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-lyn-line px-6 py-4">
          <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-lyn-ink"><%= t('marketing.hero_panel.title') %></span>
          <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-lyn-ink-soft">
            <span class="size-1.5 rounded-full bg-lyn-blue"></span>
            <%= t('marketing.hero_panel.live') %>
          </span>
        </div>

        <ul class="divide-y divide-lyn-line">
          <%# The glyph is WRITTEN HERE rather than read from the locale file, because Tailwind's icon plugin
              generates a rule only for a class it can see in a scanned file -- an icon name that lived in a
              YAML string would be purged and render as an empty square. %>
          <% [['one', 'i-lucide-message-circle'], ['two', 'i-lucide-instagram'], ['three', 'i-lucide-globe']]
               .each_with_index do |(row, icon), index| %>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3.5 px-6 py-4 <%= 'bg-lyn-mist' if index.zero? %>">
              <span class="mt-0.5 grid size-10 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-xl bg-lyn-royal/10 text-lyn-royal">
                <span class="<%= icon %> size-[1.15rem]"></span>
              </span>
              <span class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                <span class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
                  <span class="truncate text-sm font-semibold text-lyn-ink"><%= t("marketing.hero_panel.rows.#{row}.name") %></span>
                  <span class="shrink-0 text-xs text-lyn-ink-soft"><%= t("marketing.hero_panel.rows.#{row}.channel") %></span>
                </span>
                <span class="mt-1 block truncate text-sm leading-relaxed text-lyn-ink-soft">
                  <%= t("marketing.hero_panel.rows.#{row}.message") %>
                </span>
              </span>
            </li>
          <% end %>
        </ul>

        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 border-t border-lyn-line px-6 py-4">
          <span class="flex-1 rounded-xl bg-lyn-mist px-4 py-3 text-sm text-lyn-ink-soft">
            <%= t('marketing.hero_panel.composer') %>
          </span>
          <span class="grid size-10 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-xl bg-lyn-indigo text-lyn-paper">
            <span class="i-lucide-send size-[1.1rem]"></span>
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%# THE ONE LABEL, AND IT SITS CLEAR OF THE CARD. Two floating pills used to overlap the messages they
          were meant to annotate; the first attempt at one pill still had 14px of it lying across the
          composer row. The wrapper's bottom padding is the badge's own height plus its clearance, so the
          card ends where the card ends in both locales. %>
      <span class="absolute bottom-0 start-6 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-lyn-indigo px-4 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-lyn-paper shadow-[0_16px_34px_-14px_rgba(0,0,0,0.8)]">
        <span class="i-lucide-check size-3.5"></span>
        <%= t('marketing.hero_panel.badges.assigned') %>
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
